<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Sept 27.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Sept 27.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 09/27/96  09/20/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    198.70    191.71    85.44	83.07     86.60</p>
<p>West	    230.42    226.45    87.37	80.82     91.40</p>
<p>Total Canada  429.11    418.17    86.46	81.84     89.00</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 09/27/96: 232.55 bcf, 09/20/96: 230.77 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 09/27/96: 263.74 bcf, 09/20/96: 280.19 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S. -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
